 ## Overview
-Barycentric interpolation on tetrahedra reconstructs a scalar or vector field value at an arbitrary point $p$ inside a tetrahedron by computing a weighted sum of the values at the tetrahedron's four vertices, where the weights are the point's barycentric coordinates [S1, unofficial][S2, S3, S4]. It extends 2D barycentric interpolation to the 3D simplex, providing a piecewise linear, C0-continuous field over unstructured tetrahedral meshes [S1, unofficial][S2]. Unlike [Barycentric Interpolation on Triangles](5671-barycentric-interpolation-on-triangles.md), which operates on 2D surfaces, this method operates in 3D volume using four vertices, making it suitable for volumetric data sampling in [Tetrahedral Volume Rendering](1843-tetrahedral-volume-rendering.md).
